  {
   "slug": "rooms",
   "title": "Rooms & suites",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"lead\"} --><p class=\"lead\">All rooms face the sea and have handmade beds, linen from a mill up the coast, a rain shower and a tray with good coffee. Prices include breakfast for two.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns {\"align\":\"wide\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"room-card\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group room-card\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:room-harbour}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:room-harbour}}\" alt=\"The Harbour Room\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:room-harbour}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Harbour Room</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rate\"} --><p class=\"rate\">From $180 a night · sleeps 2</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A king bed, window seat and harbour view. First floor.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"{{page:book}}\">Book this room</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"room-card\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group room-card\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:room-dune}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:room-dune}}\" alt=\"The Dune Room\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:room-dune}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Dune Room</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rate\"} --><p class=\"rate\">From $165 a night · sleeps 2</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Balcony over the dunes, walk-in shower. Ground floor, step-free.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"{{page:book}}\">Book this room</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns {\"align\":\"wide\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"room-card\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group room-card\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:room-lighthouse}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:room-lighthouse}}\" alt=\"The Lighthouse Room\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:room-lighthouse}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Lighthouse Room</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rate\"} --><p class=\"rate\">From $195 a night · sleeps 2</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Corner room with two windows and a view of the light at night.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"{{page:book}}\">Book this room</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"room-card\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group room-card\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:suite-tide}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:suite-tide}}\" alt=\"The Tide Suite\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:suite-tide}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Tide Suite</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rate\"} --><p class=\"rate\">From $260 a night · sleeps 3</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Separate sitting room, deep bath and a sofa bed for a child.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:buttons --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"is-style-outline\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"{{page:book}}\">Book this room</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"align\":\"full\",\"className\":\"section-band\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull section-band\"><!-- wp:heading {\"className\":\"section-title\"} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading section-title\">In every room</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"amenities\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list amenities\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>King or twin beds with feather-free bedding on request</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Rain shower and organic bath products</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Fast Wi-Fi and a desk with a view</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Blackout blinds and a sea breeze</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Fresh milk and biscuits from the bakery</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Dogs welcome in the Dune Room</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:group -->",
   "featured_media": "room-harbour",
   "template": "page-full",
   "menu_order": 1
  },
  {
   "slug": "amenities",
   "title": "Amenities",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"lead\"} --><p class=\"lead\">A small inn means small luxuries done well.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns {\"align\":\"wide\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"feature-card\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group feature-card\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"icon\"} --><p class=\"icon\">~</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The snug</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Wood fire, board games, an honesty bar and a shelf of well-thumbed sea novels.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"feature-card\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group feature-card\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"icon\"} --><p class=\"icon\">~</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Breakfast room</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Served from eight to eleven at long tables in the old net loft.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"feature-card\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group feature-card\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"icon\"} --><p class=\"icon\">~</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Bikes &amp; boards</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Four bikes, two paddleboards and wetsuits in most sizes.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:shells}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"align\":\"wide\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large alignwide\"><img src=\"{{media:shells}}\" alt=\"Shells on sand\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:shells}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Breakfast menu</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"price-list\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list price-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Harbour breakfast</strong> <span class=\"price\">included</span> <span class=\"desc\">Eggs any way, smoked haddock or bacon, bakery toast</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Porridge</strong> <span class=\"price\">included</span> <span class=\"desc\">With honey from the cliff-top hives</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Picnic box</strong> <span class=\"price\">$18</span> <span class=\"desc\">Sandwiches, fruit and cake for the beach; order the night before</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->",
   "parent": "rooms",
   "menu_order": 2
  },
  {
   "slug": "book",
   "title": "Book a stay",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"lead\"} --><p class=\"lead\">Book directly with us for the best rate, a free bottle of local cider and flexible changes up to seven days before arrival.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns {\"align\":\"wide\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">By phone or email</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Call <a href=\"tel:+15550160011\">+1 (555) 016-0011</a> between 9 am and 8 pm, or email <a href=\"mailto:stay@driftwood.example\">stay@driftwood.example</a> with your dates and room.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Good to know</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Check-in from 3 pm, check-out by 11 am</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Two-night minimum at weekends from May to September</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Children of all ages welcome</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>One dog-friendly room</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Gift stays</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>A night by the sea makes a wonderful present. Vouchers are valid for eighteen months and can be used for any room.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "featured_media": "evening-tide",
   "template": "page-full",
   "menu_order": 3
  },
  {
   "slug": "about",
   "title": "Our story",
   "content": "<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaId\":{{media_id:harbour-boats}},\"mediaType\":\"image\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"{{media:harbour-boats}}\" alt=\"Boats in the harbour\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:harbour-boats}} size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">From net loft to inn</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>For a hundred years this building stored nets, floats and lobster pots. In 2019 we rebuilt it with reclaimed timber, lime plaster and as much glass as the planners would allow, so every room faces the water.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We are a family of four and a team of nine, most of whom grew up within a mile of the harbour.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div><!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We wanted the kind of place we would want to come home to after a long walk in the wind.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>The owners</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Looking after the coast</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We heat the inn with an air-source heat pump, buy from boats and farms within twenty miles and give every guest a bag for a two-minute beach clean.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "menu_order": 4
  },
  {
   "slug": "contact",
   "title": "Contact",
   "content": "<!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Find us</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>1 Harbour Steps, Gull Point. The inn is at the far end of the harbour wall, past the lifeboat station. Parking for guests behind the building.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Phone <a href=\"tel:+15550160011\">+1 (555) 016-0011</a><br>Email <a href=\"mailto:stay@driftwood.example\">stay@driftwood.example</a></p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:lighthouse}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:lighthouse}}\" alt=\"The lighthouse at the end of the pier\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:lighthouse}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->",
   "menu_order": 5
  }
 ],
 "posts": [
  {
   "slug": "a-slow-day-at-gull-point",
   "title": "A slow day at Gull Point",
   "date": "2026-10-20T08:30:00",
   "excerpt": "Sunrise on the sand, coffee on the harbour wall and a long walk to the lighthouse: our favourite unhurried day.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Guests often ask us how to spend a single day here. Our answer is always the same: slowly. This is the day we would plan for ourselves.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Morning</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Walk down to the water before breakfast, when the sand is still smooth and the gulls have the beach to themselves. Low tide uncovers the rock pools at the north end.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Afternoon</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Take the cliff path to the lighthouse (an hour each way).</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Stop at the tea hut halfway for a slice of lemon cake.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Come back along the beach if the tide is out.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:lighthouse}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:lighthouse}}\" alt=\"The lighthouse at the end of the pier\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:lighthouse}}\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The light still turns every night.</figcaption></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Evening</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Watch the boats come in from the harbour wall, then settle in the snug with a glass of something local while the fire does its work.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "walks"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "autumn",
    "coast"
   ],
   "featured_media": "cliff-path",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": true,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Marta",
     "email": "marta@example.com",
     "content": "We did exactly this last month and it was the best day of our holiday.",
     "date": "2026-10-22T20:15:00"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "slug": "best-rock-pools",
   "title": "The best rock pools, and how to visit them kindly",
   "date": "2026-10-08T09:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Crabs, anemones and the occasional starfish. Where to look, when to go and what to leave behind.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The rocks at the north end of the bay hold some of the best pools on this stretch of coast. Go an hour either side of low tide and you will have plenty of time.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What you might find</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Beadlet anemones, like red jelly sweets</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Shore crabs hiding under weed</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Blennies darting between stones</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Periwinkles and limpets on every rock</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Look with your eyes first. Most of the best finds are sitting perfectly still.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Our youngest guide, aged nine</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Please put every stone back the way you found it, and keep anything you catch in a bucket of seawater for a few minutes only. Buckets and nets are in the porch.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "beaches"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "families",
    "nature"
   ],
   "featured_media": "shells",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "where-to-eat-in-the-harbour",
   "title": "Where to eat in the harbour",
   "date": "2026-09-27T18:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Fish and chips on the wall, a proper oyster bar and the best breakfast that is not ours.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>We serve breakfast, but for lunch and dinner we happily send guests to our neighbours. These are the places we eat on our nights off.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"price-list\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list price-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>The Net Shed</strong> <span class=\"price\">$$</span> <span class=\"desc\">Crab sandwiches and chowder at the end of the quay</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Harbour Fish Bar</strong> <span class=\"price\">$</span> <span class=\"desc\">Chips on the wall, with gulls for company</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>The Oyster Room</strong> <span class=\"price\">$$$</span> <span class=\"desc\">Local oysters and a short wine list; book ahead</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Saltwater Bakery</strong> <span class=\"price\">$</span> <span class=\"desc\">Cardamom buns from seven in the morning</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Most places close early in winter, so ring ahead from November. We are always happy to book a table for you.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>On a fine evening, nothing beats a paper parcel of fish and chips eaten on the harbour wall while the light goes pink over the water.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "food-drink"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "local"
   ],
   "featured_media": "harbour-boats",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "swimming-in-autumn",
   "title": "Swimming in autumn: a beginner's guide",
   "date": "2026-09-15T07:30:00",
   "excerpt": "The sea is warmest in September. A gentle guide to your first autumn dip.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Here is a secret that locals know: the sea is warmer in September than in June. If you have ever wanted to try cold-water swimming, autumn is the gentlest place to start.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Before you go in</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Swim between the flags when the lifeguards are on</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Never swim alone; we can introduce you to the morning swim group</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Wear a bright hat and take a warm drink for afterwards</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Walk in slowly, breathe out long and steady, and stay in for just a few minutes the first time. Getting warm afterwards matters more than how long you swam.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Towels, a hot-water bottle and a flask of hot chocolate are waiting by the back door for any guest who asks.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "beaches"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "autumn",
    "swimming"
   ],
   "featured_media": "evening-tide",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Ben",
     "email": "ben@example.com",
     "content": "Joined the morning swimmers on Saturday. Freezing, wonderful, will be back.",
     "date": "2026-09-21T11:40:00"
    }
   ]
