  {
   "slug": "dunes-walk",
   "title": "A circular walk through the dunes",
   "date": "2026-09-01T10:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Five miles of soft paths, skylarks and sea views, finishing at a pub with a garden.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>This is our favourite walk for a bright, breezy day. It is mostly flat, but soft sand makes it feel longer than five miles, so allow three hours.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The route</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Start at the inn and follow the beach north for a mile.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Turn inland at the lifeguard hut onto the boardwalk.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Follow the marker posts through the dunes to the old church.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Return by the river path and stop at the pub garden.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Keep dogs on a lead from March to July, when skylarks nest in the grass. We lend out maps and binoculars from the hall.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>There is a bench at the highest dune with a view along the whole bay; it is the perfect place for the picnic box we can pack for you the night before.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "walks"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "nature"
   ],
   "featured_media": "dunes",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  },
  {
   "slug": "new-suite-opens",
   "title": "The Tide Suite is open",
   "date": "2026-08-20T12:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Our largest room yet, with a deep bath by the window and a view all the way to the lighthouse.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>After a winter of careful building, the old sail loft at the top of the inn has become our ninth room: the Tide Suite.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:suite-tide}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:suite-tide}}\" alt=\"The Tide Suite with a big window over the water\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:suite-tide}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is inside</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A king bed facing the window</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A deep bath you can see the sea from</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A sitting room with a sofa bed</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A record player and a small library</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Book before the end of October and we will add a bottle of cider and a picnic box to your first day.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The suite sleeps three, with a sofa bed in the sitting room, and is reached by its own staircase, so it feels like a small cottage at the top of the house.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "inn-news"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "local"
   ],
   "featured_media": "suite-tide",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": false
  }
